-- #1617 CONTROL — main.mdk's shape with the two FUNCTION types replaced by two
-- `data` types, so both impl heads are real tycons. ONE dimension flips: the
-- kind of the head. Same interface, same two impls in the same order, same
-- bodies, same call shape.
--
-- If this stays green while main.mdk reproduces, the trigger is the
-- function-typed head and not "two impls of one interface".
--
-- Per #1144 this harness grades a control on its EXIT CODE ONLY, and a
-- wrong-value-at-exit-0 defect cannot be discriminated by an exit code unless
-- the program puts the value into the exit code. So `main` ASSERTS (5, 9) and
-- panics otherwise rather than printing it — a control that merely printed
-- would exit 0 either way and could never fail. PROVEN ABLE TO FAIL: changing
-- the comparand to a value the program cannot produce, `(5, 99)`, makes
-- `medaka run control.mdk` exit 1 with `runtime error [E-PANIC]: control
-- regressed: ...` (measured 2026-08-14).
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int
data W = W
data V = V
impl Sz W where
  sz _ = 5
impl Sz V where
  sz _ = 9
main =
  if (sz W, sz V) == (5, 9)
    then println "control-ok:(5, 9)"
    else panic "control regressed: two impls at two DATA-typed heads no longer dispatch to (5, 9)"
